# Checkpoint → listen infer (mandatory)

When training, fine-tuning, or promoting produces a **new** `best.pt` / `last.pt`
(Talker, mel baseline, variance, vocoder, tokenizer decode, or similar):

1. **Do not stop at train metrics alone.** Immediately run a listen-demo infer
   and leave wavs under `out/<run>_listen_demo/` (mirror to Windows `out/` when
   the job ran in WSL).
2. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/checkpoint-listen/SKILL.md`.
3. Tell the user the **exact paths** to play (stock vs new side-by-side when
   comparing vocoders or duration modes).
4. Skip only if the user explicitly says not to synthesize.

Default mel Talker demo:

```bash
python scripts/28_infer_mel.py \
  --ckpt runs/<run>/best.pt \
  --demo \
  --duration-mode mean_stats \
  --gap-mode expand_neighbor \
  --out out/<run>_listen_demo
```

Vocoder FT: pass `--vocoder-ckpt runs/<vocoder_run>/best.pt` and also keep a
stock baseline folder for A/B.
